* MiCA Title II\nOther crypto-assets
** Triggers
*** Offer to the public (Art. 4): offeror
*** Admission to trading (Art. 5): person seeking admission
*** Offeror must be a legal person
*** One white paper for all EU offers and listings
** Exemptions (Art. 4)
*** 4(2): white paper waived
**** < 150 persons per Member State
**** ≤ EUR 1 000 000 in 12 months
**** Qualified investors only
*** 4(3): outside Title II
**** Offered for free (no data, no fee)
**** Protocol rewards (mining, staking)
**** Utility token for a live service
**** Limited network of merchants
*** Lost on any listing announcement (4(4))
** White paper (Art. 6, Annex I)
*** Ten information blocks, Parts A–I
*** Climate impact of consensus mechanism
*** First-page "not approved" statement
*** Risk statement, no future-value claims
*** Management-body statement
*** Summary, languages, machine-readable
** Marketing (Art. 7)
*** Identified, consistent, fixed statement
*** Not before publication of the white paper
** Notification and publication (Arts 8–9)
*** Home authority, 20 working days ahead
*** No prior approval (8(3))
*** Own classification analysis (8(4))
*** ESMA register (Art. 109)
*** EU-wide right to offer (Art. 11)
** After publication
*** Results and custody of funds (Art. 10)
*** Modifications, 7 working days (Art. 12)
*** Conduct obligations (Art. 14)
** Holder protection
*** 14-day retail withdrawal (Art. 13)
*** Not for tokens already listed
*** Liability of offeror and board (Art. 15)
*** No contractual exclusion
** Transition (Art. 143)
*** Offers ended before 30 Dec. 2024: exempt
*** Old listings: white paper by 31 Dec. 2027
@endmindmap
